course: dictionary
lesson: 10666
title: Unlikely: probably not, or surprising
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unlikely means probably not going to happen, or probably not true. «It is unlikely to snow in summer in Sydney.» Summer in Sydney is hot, so snow probably will not happen. The words summer and Sydney are the clues.
explain: Unlikely can also mean surprising, or not what you would expect. In «an unlikely hero», the hero is someone small or shy who saves the day. Nobody expects the shy one to win, so the hero is unlikely in a surprising way.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in «probably not». «It is probably not going to snow in summer in Sydney» still makes sense, so unlikely means probably not here. Look for phrases too: «highly unlikely» means very unlikely, and «unlikely to» is followed by a verb, like «unlikely to win».
fact: Unlikely means probably not going to happen, or not what you would expect.
fact: «Highly unlikely» means very unlikely, and «in the unlikely event» means if something rare happens.
fact: In maths, chance is shown on a scale: impossible, unlikely, even chance, likely, certain.
fact: «An unlikely hero» is someone small or shy who surprises everyone by doing something great.
fact: Unlikely is an adjective: more unlikely, most unlikely.
exercise: «It is unlikely to snow in summer in Sydney.» What does unlikely mean here? | *Probably not going to happen | Certain to happen | Fun to watch | Happening every single day
exercise: «An unlikely hero» saves the day. What does unlikely suggest about the hero? | *Surprising, not what you would expect | Tall and strong | Probably not going to happen | Loud and bossy
exercise: On the chance scale, which word sits between impossible and even chance? | Impossible | Likely | Certain | *Unlikely
test: «No humans have yet gone to Mars, and a crewed landing is unlikely before the 2030s.» What does unlikely mean here? | Surprising and exciting | Impossible to see | *Probably not going to happen before then | Happening very soon
test: Choose the best phrase: «It is ___ that the shop will be open at midnight.» | Completely sure | *Highly unlikely | Definitely | Certain
exam: What is the opposite of unlikely on the chance scale? | Unlikely again | *Likely | Impossible | Quiet
